meta {
  name: Providers - List
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/ai-providers
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
}

docs {
  The providers a workspace can bring its own key for (bring your own
  key), from `config('byok.providers')`. Requires `ai-credential.view`.

  Each entry carries `key` (the `execution_provider` value
  `Provider Credentials - Create` expects), `label`, `key_url`,
  `key_placeholder`, `key_prefix`, `key_guide`, the catalog `models` that
  key would run, and `covers_knowledge_base` (true for the embeddings
  provider).

  `can_add_team` / `can_add_personal` say what the caller may add —
  personal keys also need the workspace policy's `allow_personal_keys`.

  Response is wrapped:
  `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { providers, can_add_team, can_add_personal } }`.
}
